    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2d4ca7de",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts Adolf Hitler on the phone, with overlaid text that reads: 'I'm responsible for the deaths of over 50 million people!' and 'so another dozen or so won't hurt! *click!*'. This meme uses the historical figure of Hitler, a symbol of genocide and mass murder, to create a darkly humorous and grotesque analogy. The intent is to mock the idea of someone being indifferent to massive loss of life, by juxtaposing the image of Hitler with a callous, casual attitude toward death. This is a hateful meme because it trivializes the Holocaust and the immense suffering caused by Hitler's regime, reducing a horrific historical atrocity to a joke. It also implicitly glorifies or normalizes the mindset of a mass murderer, which is deeply offensive and harmful. The meme is not targeted at a specific group based on protected characteristics, but it is hateful in its glorification of evil and its mockery of the gravity of genocide. The overall intent is to provoke shock and dark humor by equating the scale of human suffering with a casual, almost mundane, attitude.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b38f72f8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
